title: awa-ssh 0.3.1 static-auth-db constraint vs. Pricklypear's authd-RPC auth model
section: supervisor.ssh-interface
kind: implementation-discovery
status: open

body: |
  DISCOVERED in iteration 21 while building the awa-ssh real-SSH swap-in
  (deferred since it6; feasibility spike proved in it15):
  The poohstack opam switch currently has awa/awa-mirage 0.3.1 installed.
  At this version, `Awa.Server.make : Awa.Hostkey.priv -> Awa.Auth.db
  -> Awa.Server.t * Awa.Ssh.message list` takes the FULL user database
  (list of {name; password option; keys}) STATICALLY at server-make time.
  There is NO per-connection auth-event callback hook — the SSH handshake
  verifies the client pubkey/password against this in-memory db.

  This conflicts with Pricklypear's architecture: spec [auth.section]
  says auth lives in a SEPARATE unikernel (authd) and the supervisor
  calls verify_ssh_key via HTTP RPC. The supervisor does not have the
  user/key set in memory; authd does.

  PR #74 in upstream awa-ssh (merged April 2025, released in 0.5.x) fixes
  exactly this: "Userauth is now an event. This means the effectful layer
  can do e.g. database lookups or LDAP requests when authenticating a
  user." With 0.5.x, we'd register an auth callback that calls authd's
  /verify_ssh_key per-connection — clean and idiomatic.

  The 0.3.1 → 0.5.x upgrade cascade is significant (opam dry-run shows
  21 upgrades, 3 removals, 4 installs including mirage-crypto-pk 0.11->2.1,
  mirage-crypto-rng 0.11->2.1, tls, x509, tcpip major-version bumps).
  These cascade into auth/, which uses mirage-crypto for the existing
  HMAC token machinery. AGENTS.md says "Do not add dependencies lightly";
  this upgrade deserves its own focused iteration with careful audit,
  not bundling into the SSH swap-in.

  WORKAROUND in v1 (built this iteration):
  - Keep the awa-ssh 0.3.1 stack installed (no upgrade).
  - Supervisor builds the Awa.Auth.db at startup by querying authd's new
    /list_ssh_credentials endpoint (which returns all (username, ssh_key)
    pairs from the credentials table). This is a startup-only snapshot;
    runtime key rotation requires a supervisor restart until awa-ssh 0.5.x.
  - Acceptable for v1 (personal/small-team per spec [auth.bootstrap-admin]).
    New admin keys added later will require `supervisor restart` — same
    blast radius as the OpenSSH model's "reload" on authorized_keys edit.

  RECOMMENDED RESOLUTION:
  - Plan-pass: leave supervisor.ssh-interface at `partial` until the
    0.5.x upgrade is shipped; document the snapshot-refresh caveat
    in the section's agent note.
  - When 0.5.x is upgraded: rewrite `ssh_awa.ml`'s db build to a
    single per-connection auth callback that calls authd's
    /verify_ssh_key — eliminates the snapshot refresh concern.
